{
  "version": 1,
  "note": [
    "The odd-jar ladder (Design System §8, signed at Gate A §8.1) as a DATA SET.",
    "Rarity is declared as a MEAN INTERVAL IN HOURS, never as a raw weight — a weight",
    "is only meaningful once you also know the belt's jar rate, and nobody reading a",
    "weight can tell whether it means 'twice a shift' or 'never'. The loop converts an",
    "interval to a per-jar probability using the belt's own measured rate, so changing",
    "the belt speed or the jar pitch cannot silently re-tune the whole ladder.",
    "Verify with: node tools/jar-rarity.mjs"
  ],
